# Reuse functions

Search the repo before writing a function. If one already does the job, call it.

A private function still counts. Make it public, or move it to a shared module, and call it. Do not copy the body under a new name.

```elixir
# BAD — Direct.require_admin/1 already allows admin and reviewer
defp require_roster_staff(uid) do
  Repo.query("... role_id IN ('admin', 'reviewer')", [uid])
end

# GOOD — call the existing check
:ok <- Direct.require_admin(uid)
```

Add a function only when no existing one can take the difference as an argument.
